This cartridge is MADFAM's own authoring. It implements the published
INTERFACE DIMENSIONS of four shop / desk organization grids so that parts
built for one system mount on another. It reproduces no upstream geometry,
vendors no upstream file, and derives from no upstream implementation.

The standards implemented
-------------------------

Multiboard (25 mm grid)                     [ADR-021 section 4: interface-only]
  Author:    Keep Making Limited (Jonathan, "Keep Making")
  Source:    https://www.multiboard.io/ (now redirects to https://multibuild.io/)
             Licence page: https://multibuild.io/license (read 2026-09-05)
  Standard:  The 25 mm cell pitch, the ~12.4 mm core hole and the 4 mm plate
             corner radius — the dimensions a part must honour to mount on a
             Multiboard board.
  Form:      OURS. The `multiboard_tile` mode (multiboard_field() in main.py)
             is a plain filleted plate carrying one plain circular hole per
             cell. It does NOT reproduce the distinctive Multiboard tile form:
             there is no hex or petal cell profile, no snap ring, no thread
             profile, and no other element of the Multiboard tile's expression.
             The geometry was written for this cartridge from the interface
             dimensions alone.
  Note:      The Multiboard design as published by Keep Making is licensed for
             personal, NON-COMMERCIAL use only, with a separate commercial
             licence required to sell derivatives (the A1 provenance audit
             records this as CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0; the publisher's own licence page
             would not serve to an automated reader on 2026-09-05, so the exact
             SPDX variant is recorded here as the audit found it and the
             verified fact is the NC restriction). Either way that licence is
             incompatible with this commons, and it covers Keep Making's
             DESIGN. It is not implicated here:
             this cartridge implements the interface's measurements, which are
             facts of fit and not copyrightable expression, with a form of its
             own — the acceptance target ADR-021 section 4 sets for Multiboard
             compatibility. No Multiboard model, source file or export was
             consulted, copied or adapted in authoring this mode. (Ruled
             2026-09-05; see the operator checklist, item G20.)

Gridfinity (42 mm grid)
  Author:    Zack Freedman (Voidstar Lab)
  Source:    https://gridfinity.xyz/
  License:   MIT License
  Standard:  The 42 mm grid module and the standard baseplate chamfer stack,
             implemented as a socket. A published standard, not code.

French cleat (45 degrees)
  Source:    An unowned woodworking shop convention; no author and no licence.
  Standard:  The 45-degree interlocking rail profile.

Pegboard (1 in pitch, 1/4 in holes)
  Source:    An unowned shop convention; no author and no licence.
  Standard:  The US 1 in (25.4 mm) hole pitch and 1/4 in (6.35 mm) hole
             diameter a pegboard hook must honour (PEG_PITCH / PEG_HOLE_D in
             main.py).

Libraries
---------

None. This cartridge is a single CadQuery mode set (main.py) and uses no
OpenSCAD library and no third-party Python package beyond CadQuery itself.
